**Read:** [Hazards of oxygen-deficient atmospheres — EIGA 44/18](../sources/Oxygen-Deficient-Atmospheres-EIGA.lingua#r_0KCKFEBVRBMZNF4KQ9PSXB9QCA), monitoring and response; [Fatal liquid nitrogen release — CSB Foundation Food Group investigation](../sources/Foundation-Food-Group-Investigation-CSB.lingua#r_7KXAYPC80QQ764WA8DKSJTDRGA), atmosphere and emergency-preparedness analysis.

A cold gas cloud warms, entrains air and moves through a geometry with obstacles and openings. Its composition need not equal a room average. A detector samples a location and responds over time; a correct sensor can miss an unobserved region or report after conditions have changed there.

Separate transport delay, instrument response, alarm recognition and the time required for an effective action. For an illustrative sensor τs dz/dt=y−z, even a known step in local composition takes time to appear in z. In an actual installation the gas field is itself evolving, and a sample tube can add another inventory and delay.

**Work:** Compare an ideal instantaneous detector with the first-order model, then add a transport delay. Identify observations needed to validate detector placement and response. Keep spatial uncertainty distinct from calibration uncertainty; neither can be repaired by assuming the other is small.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies — from molecules to useful service](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
